{
 "notes": ["The hangar's ASSEMBLE (original scene 4: setup 0x01b295, the grid 0x019a3e drawn by 0x01877e, the side choice 0x01b78f drawn by 0x017af0, the lists 0x01b59d drawn by 0x018d50 and the row drawers 0x1dae38, the details 0x01b482 drawn by 0x019d24, fitting 0x01afe1, DIS 0x01ade0). The hangar's menu opens it for the hangar chosen; EXIT goes back to the menu.", "The grid's twelve cells, column by column, top first: BODY, LEG, ARM, CHIP, BACK, COLOR, OPTION, STICKER, NAME, DIS, SPEC, EXIT. The icons slide in over slide_seconds; left/right (sys 4) and up/down (sys 3) move without wrapping, cancel jumps to EXIT (sys 4). A cell that cannot be chosen wears the disabled mark (sys 8 on confirm): NAME and SPEC without a body, legs and CHIP, DIS with nothing fitted, COLOR for a robot of makers 3 to 6 (unpaintable_makers).", "ARM and BACK first ask which side (sys 4; side 0 is the right-hand weapon): the pair rises out of the cell and parts. The list shows the stock's parts of the kind, and the paints and emblems owned, by name; X sorts by name and Y by price (sys 5); up/down move (sys 3). A line is grey when it cannot be fitted: another hangar holds it, a weapon is on the other side, a module needs more sockets than are free, or (same_maker) its maker is not the robot's. Gold is fitted here; confirm opens its details, confirm again fits it (sys 29) or, fitted already, takes it off. A body with fewer socket holes than the modules take has them all taken off with the modules_off notice.", "DIS asks the dismantle question (NO chosen; left/right sys 4): YES takes every part off (sys 41). A hangar left without a body, legs or CHIP loses its name and stops being ridden. NAME opens NAME ENTRY for the Scoobee's name; SPEC the SV SPEC screen.", "Researcher readings: the chosen row's place in the details, the cells' help. The panel turns the hangar's Scoobee as fitted so far, standing or its parts one by one (0x08371b), through robot_preview.json's assemble entry. A CHIP or a module has no maker: 0x01ede8 gives a body, legs or weapon its record's maker and anything else 7, which the lists draw without a badge, and the fitting check (0x0186e9) passes any line whose maker or the robot's (scene +0x3628) is 7, so as in the original they fit any robot.", "details.totals up_colour and down_colour (port addition, opt-in, absent by default): a value the part raises or lowers, and its arrow (3603 up, 3602 down), take that colour, for example \"up_colour\": \"#5aa0ff\", \"down_colour\": \"#ff5050\" in a mod's ui/assemble.json. Without them both stay in colour, as the original draws them (0x0179ed)."],
